  "plan": {
    "goal": "Design a kidney compartment on a body-on-chip (70 kg adult, cardiac output 5000 mL/min, 5e6 chip cells in 30 µL) that matches the in-vivo renal transit time of ~5 s.",
    "rationale": "The chip flow is chosen so that the mean residence (transit) time in the 30 µL kidney compartment equals the in-vivo renal transit of ~5 s: Q = V/t = 30 µL / 5 s = 6 µL/s = 360 µL/min. The scaling calculator then derives the organ flow fraction (kidneys ≈ 20% of cardiac output in vivo), the scaled organ flow rate, the cells-in-organ (allometric scaling from body mass), and the resulting transit time. Assumptions: 70 kg adult, cardiac output 5000 mL/min, kidneys receive ~20% of cardiac output in vivo, chip holds 5e6 cells in 30 µL.",
